course: dictionary
lesson: 7215
title: Phoenician
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Words ending in -ian often tell you where something comes from or who belongs to a place. Phoenician means belonging to Phoenicia, an ancient land on the coast of what is now Lebanon. «The Phoenicians were sea-traders from cities such as Tyre, Sidon and Byblos.» So the cities came from Phoenicia, and the people who lived there were Phoenicians.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «The Phoenicians spread a 22-letter alphabet around the Mediterranean.» The Mediterranean is a sea, and sea-traders sail on seas, so the Phoenicians travelled and traded by ship. Ask: what word would fit here? Then test your meaning: "sea-traders from Lebanon spread a 22-letter alphabet" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Phoenician can work as a describing word or as a noun. In «the Phoenician alphabet», Phoenician describes the alphabet and means it came from Phoenicia. In «Phoenicians were famous for a costly purple dye», Phoenicians means the people themselves.
fact: Phoenicia was an ancient land of trading cities on the coast of what is now Lebanon.
fact: Tyre, Sidon and Byblos were Phoenician cities.
fact: «Phoenician» can describe a thing from Phoenicia, and «Phoenicians» are the people from there.
fact: The Phoenician alphabet had letters for sounds, and Greek, Latin and our ABC came from it.
fact: The Phoenicians were famous for a costly purple dye made from sea snails.
exercise: «The Phoenicians were sea-traders from cities such as Tyre, Sidon and Byblos.» What is a Phoenician? | A kind of purple dye | A type of sea snail | A trading ship made of stone | *A person from Phoenicia
exercise: In «the Phoenician alphabet», what does Phoenician tell us? | *The alphabet came from Phoenicia | The alphabet was spoken by sea snails | The alphabet was written in purple | The alphabet was only for numbers
exercise: Which of these came from the Phoenician alphabet? | A purple sea snail | A costly purple dye | The Sahara desert | *Our ABC
test: «The Phoenicians spread their alphabet around the Mediterranean.» Where did the alphabet spread? | Only inside one small town | Around the moon | Under the ground | *Around the Mediterranean Sea
test: Which word in «Phoenicians were famous for a costly purple dye» names the people? | costly | *Phoenicians | famous | dye
exam: «The Phoenician alphabet had letters for sounds, and Greek and Latin came from it.» What does Phoenician mean here? | A kind of sea snail | A word meaning very old and broken | *Belonging to Phoenicia, an ancient land on the coast of Lebanon | A famous purple colour
